       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision (2,400 mg/day is the more common ceiling). A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory regimen.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum.\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), or **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, if that was the intended daily amount. This could be 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also want a note on the order giving the rationale."
