       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this one as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is well above the maximum labeled dose. It adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, because the drug has a ceiling effect. It does substantially raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. You haven't given a clinical rationale that would justify that risk, so I can't treat this as an intentional deviation.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note if you want one.\n- **Enter a lower dose** such as 600 to 800 mg PO three times daily.\n- **Add a second agent**, such as scheduled acetaminophen, if the goal is stronger analgesia. I can enter that too.\n\nIf you believe there's a special circumstance that requires this dose, please discuss it with the pharmacy or clinical pharmacology service. The order would then need to go through your institution's high-dose override process, not through me.\n\nLet me know which of the options above you'd like and I'll enter it."
